(3032767, 425451, 66223, '<td valign="top">nice picture, i really like it... i''ll give it a 9!  great texture on the wrapper.  however these are fakes. the real cuban cohibas have a similar band with squares and not dots (<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.cigaraficionado.com/Cigar/Graphics/Counterfeit/cohiba_genuine.gif'', strrpos(''//www.cigaraficionado.com/Cigar/Graphics/Counterfeit/cohiba_genuine.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.cigaraficionado.com/Cigar/Graphics/Counterfeit/cohiba_genuine.gif"/>).  the non-cuban cohiba brand is produced by general cigar and has a band that does not at all look like the cuban ones (<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.cigaraficionado.com/Cigar/Graphics/Counterfeit/count_co-dr1_lrg.gif'', strrpos(''//www.cigaraficionado.com/Cigar/Graphics/Counterfeit/count_co-dr1_lrg.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.cigaraficionado.com/Cigar/Graphics/Counterfeit/count_co-dr1_lrg.gif"/>).  these dominican ones that have bands that are similar to the cuban ones are fakes...</td>', 'nice picture, i really like it... i''ll give it a 9!  great texture on the wrapper.  however these are fakes. the real cuban cohibas have a similar band with squares and not dots ().  the non-cuban cohiba brand is produced by general cigar and has a band that does not at all look like the cuban ones ().  these dominican ones that have bands that are similar to the cuban ones are fakes...', '2006-11-15 00:51:44.000000', NULL, 1),
