(3039628, 427112, 30049, '<td valign="top">Now this is interesting and fun to look at.  I wish the image used the full 640 to get a better look.  Seems to be a little soft (not sharply focused).  The exposure could be moved up some, but you may risk blowing out some of the ''spots'' then.  Anyway, good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Now this is interesting and fun to look at.  I wish the image used the full 640 to get a better look.  Seems to be a little soft (not sharply focused).  The exposure could be moved up some, but you may risk blowing out some of the ''spots'' then.  Anyway, good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 08:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039631, 425572, 30049, '<td valign="top">Cool water spray.  Bet this was fun to watch.  The spray is interesting, but the image could be a little better focused IMO and the water in the center of the image is a bit hot (overexposed).  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Cool water spray.  Bet this was fun to watch.  The spray is interesting, but the image could be a little better focused IMO and the water in the center of the image is a bit hot (overexposed).  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 08:46:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039635, 427519, 30049, '<td valign="top">A unique use of dice for this challenge.  Kudos for being different.  The B/W tone is good as is the clarity of the photo.  Composition is "ok".  I like the empty space showing around the hand in various places, the alignment of the dice feels unbalanced for some reason.  Sorry I can''t be more specific - hard to explain I guess.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'A unique use of dice for this challenge.  Kudos for being different.  The B/W tone is good as is the clarity of the photo.  Composition is "ok".  I like the empty space showing around the hand in various places, the alignment of the dice feels unbalanced for some reason.  Sorry I can''t be more specific - hard to explain I guess.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 08:50:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039644, 427302, 30049, '<td valign="top">Looks to be beyond "wounded" to me.  :D  Nothing personal, but it''s a little close to being kind of disgusting.  I know it''s only a bug, but still...  As for the technicals, I think the composition is a little too tight, and the lighting is a bit harsh on the left.  Color saturation is ok, getting some yellow bleed over onto the bugs shell casing.  All of the above is JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Looks to be beyond "wounded" to me.  :D  Nothing personal, but it''s a little close to being kind of disgusting.  I know it''s only a bug, but still...  As for the technicals, I think the composition is a little too tight, and the lighting is a bit harsh on the left.  Color saturation is ok, getting some yellow bleed over onto the bugs shell casing.  All of the above is JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 08:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039649, 427561, 30049, '<td valign="top">Certainly have some spots.  :D  I wish the exposure time was either longer or shorter.  The short motion trails of the stars make it look blurry.  Longer would show intentional, shorter would be cooler (if possible).  The red sky is nice as a background.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Certainly have some spots.  :D  I wish the exposure time was either longer or shorter.  The short motion trails of the stars make it look blurry.  Longer would show intentional, shorter would be cooler (if possible).  The red sky is nice as a background.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 08:55:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039653, 427160, 30049, '<td valign="top">Tricky.  :D  In trying to determine if the "giraffe" was looking away or at the viewer I had to look close.  Then I noticed that this is all a setup.  :P  The lack of any hair detail, some shine on the "face", and lack of a tail kind of gave it away.  The background is either way overexposed, or the saturation levels have been pushed beyond recovery.</td>', 'Tricky.  :D  In trying to determine if the "giraffe" was looking away or at the viewer I had to look close.  Then I noticed that this is all a setup.  :P  The lack of any hair detail, some shine on the "face", and lack of a tail kind of gave it away.  The background is either way overexposed, or the saturation levels have been pushed beyond recovery.', '2006-11-17 08:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039662, 425630, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is neat in an abstract way.  The footprints add authenticity to the photo.  Not sure what the "spots" are, but it''s fun to try and figure out.  :D  I''ve seen this drop-shadow framing in a couple of challenges now.  It''s unusual enough that you''re going to start giving yourself away, that is, if I''m correct in assuming it''s the same person doing it.  :P  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is neat in an abstract way.  The footprints add authenticity to the photo.  Not sure what the "spots" are, but it''s fun to try and figure out.  :D  I''ve seen this drop-shadow framing in a couple of challenges now.  It''s unusual enough that you''re going to start giving yourself away, that is, if I''m correct in assuming it''s the same person doing it.  :P  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 09:00:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(3039667, 427460, 30049, '<td valign="top">Nice composition in placing of the subject in the framing of this photo.  Need way more light, and the eyes are a little too blurry for maximum impact.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Nice composition in placing of the subject in the framing of this photo.  Need way more light, and the eyes are a little too blurry for maximum impact.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-17 09:02:02.000000', NULL, 1),
